  "details": "The Offline Invites to PC-only world fails if the receiver uses the Android mobile client on their last login. It should not be so because the receiver can use the PC client to respond to the invite.\n\n# Repro steps\n\n1. Prepare two accounts. I call them the sender and the receiver.\n\n2. With the receiver, log in using the Android Mobile app and start the game. Then, log out and shut down the phone.\n\n3. With the receiver, open the website, log in, and keep that state.\n\n4. With the sender, log in using the Windows app. Go PC-only world.\n\n5. With the sender, open the receiver page from social. And send an invite.\n\n6. Then, an alert will appear. That shows a message: \"You can't invite a mobile user to a PC-only world. Try going to a cross-platform world a...\".\n\n# Note\n\n- The string must be 34872 `You can't invite a mobile user to a PC-only world. Try going to a cross-platform world and inviting them.`\n\n- Tested with 2024.3.2 Build 1504 (both PC and Android mobile)",
